ok":true,"is_bank":false,"flags":[{"label":"Business quality","value":69.5,"unit":"/100","status":"ok","read":"Average quality (70/100).","meaning":"Composite of profitability, return on capital, balance-sheet safety and cash conversion (the Fundamentals-tab Quality score).","why_useful":"A durable, high-return business compounds value; a low-quality one needs a bigger margin of safety.","why_it_can_fail":"A single composite can mask a weak component; open the Fundamentals tab for the breakdown."},{"label":"Cash conversion","value":2.02,"unit":"\u00d7","status":"good","read":"2.02\u00d7 of profit came in as operating cash (5-yr median) \u2014 well backed.","meaning":"Median of (cash from operations \u00f7 net profit) over the last 5 years.","why_useful":"Profit you can't collect as cash is fragile; >0.8\u00d7 means earnings are real cash, <0.6\u00d7 is an accrual red flag.","why_it_can_fail":"One-off working-capital swings or a capex year can distort a single ratio; the 5-yr median smooths it."},{"label":"Balance-sheet safety","value":0.14,"unit":"\u00d7 D/E","status":"good","read":"Conservatively financed (D/E 0.14\u00d7, interest cover 4.1\u00d7).","meaning":"Latest debt-to-equity and interest coverage (EBIT \u00f7 interest) from the balance sheet.","why_useful":"Low debt and high interest cover let a business survive a downturn; high debt amplifies trouble.","why_it_can_fail":"Off-balance-sheet leases/guarantees aren't captured; a cash-rich firm can show low D/E yet still be risky elsewhere."},{"label":"Earnings momentum","value":-29.17,"unit":"% YoY","status":"weak","read":"Profit down 29% YoY (latest TTM).","meaning":"Trailing-twelve-month net profit vs the year-ago TTM (and whether the YoY rate is rising = 'accelerating').","why_useful":"Improving, accelerating earnings tend to drive re-rating; falling profit warns of a deteriorating business.","why_it_can_fail":"TTM can be lumpy for cyclicals/one-offs; cross-check the multi-year trend on the Fundamentals tab."}]},"valuation":{"ok":true,"is_bank":false,"pe_now":37.5,"pe_percentile":77.0,"median_pe":33.3,"earnings_yield_pct":2.67,"pb":2.32,"ev_ebitda":16.77,"quality_score":70.0,"pat_cagr_5y_pct":8.4,"peg":4.44,"cheapness":{"status":"weak","read":"P/E at the 77-percentile of its 10-yr range \u2014 expensive vs its own history."},"expectations":"At 37.5\u00d7 earnings for ~8% 5-yr profit CAGR, the market is paying \u22484.44\u00d7 growth (PEG). >2 = a lot already priced in; <1 = cheap if growth holds. This PEG divides TTM P/E by TRAILING 5-year annual PAT CAGR (endpoint-to-endpoint) \u2014 a time-axis mismatch vs the textbook FORWARD-EPS PEG, and one abnormal base/terminal year distorts the CAGR. A rough trailing valuation-vs-growth gauge, not a precise forward PEG.","cyclical_caveat":null,"meaning":"P/E percentile = where today's price-to-earnings sits within the stock's own last-10-yr range (low = cheap vs its past). Paired with the Quality score and 5-yr profit growth so a cheap multiple is judged against business strength, not in isolation.","why_useful":"Cheapness only matters relative to quality and growth \u2014 a low P/E on a declining or peak-cyclical business is a trap, not a bargain.","why_it_can_fail":"P/E breaks for loss-makers / one-offs; for banks use P/B not EV/EBITDA; a multiple cheap vs history can stay cheap if the business has structurally de-rated."},"ownership":{"ok":true,"na":null,"holders":{"Promoter":{"periods":["Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],"values":[70.14,70.14,70.15,70.15],"latest_pct":70.15,"chg_1y_pp":0.01},"FII":{"periods":["Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],"values":[3.36,3.21,2.93,2.98],"latest_pct":2.98,"chg_1y_pp":-0.38},"DII":{"periods":["Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],"values":[10.95,10.16,10.29,10.36],"latest_pct":10.36,"chg_1y_pp":-0.59},"Public":{"periods":["Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],"values":[15.55,16.49,16.63,16.52],"latest_pct":16.52,"chg_1y_pp":0.97}},"pledge":null,"events":[],"placeholders":[{"label":"Promoter pledge (detail)","note":"share-level pledge history \u2014 fetchable via NSE, deferred to MVP-2."},{"label":"Bulk / block deals","note":"large on-market trades \u2014 NSE feed, deferred to MVP-2."},{"label":"Insider / SAST disclosures","note":"promoter & designated-person dealings \u2014 deferred to MVP-2."},{"label":"Exchange announcements","note":"NSE/BSE filings stream \u2014 deferred to MVP-2."},{"label":"Results calendar","note":"next board-meeting / results date \u2014 deferred to MVP-2."},{"label":"Credit ratings","note":"rating-agency actions \u2014 deferred to MVP-2."}],"reads":{"Promoter":"Promoter stake up 0.01pp over ~1yr \u2192 70.15%.","FII":"FIIs reducing (-0.38pp YoY \u2192 2.98%).","DII":"DIIs reducing (-0.59pp YoY \u2192 10.36%)."},"meaning":"Quarterly shareholding (% held by Promoters / Foreign (FII) / Domestic (DII) institutions / Public) from Screener, plus exchange corporate actions tagged by materiality (High = structural: bonus/split/buyback/merger; Low = routine: dividend/AGM).","why_useful":"Rising promoter & institutional ownership and clean corporate actions are confirming signals; falling promoter stake or pledging is a governance/skin-in-the-game warning.","why_it_can_fail":"Shareholding is a lagged quarterly snapshot; promoter % can fall for benign reasons (QIP, ESOP dilution). Pledge & insider detail are deferred (placeholders below)."},"snapshot":{"dimensions":{"Market":{"verdict":"negative","score":-4,"drivers":["\u2212 Below its 200-day average (-12%) \u2014 downtrend.","\u00b7 50-day average still below the 200-day (no golden cross).","\u2212 34% below its 52-week high.","\u2212 Lagging the NIFTY 500 by -26pp over 12 months.","\u2212 In a deep drawdown (-38% from its peak)."],"rule":"Points: +1 price above its 200-day average \u00b7 +1 a golden cross (50-day \u2265 200-day) \u00b7 +1 within 10% of the 52-week high \u00b7 +1 beating the NIFTY 500 over 12 months; \u22121 for each opposite, and \u